      "detail": "Concede that the opportunity-cost argument has real teeth — burning 8-12% of runway per month with zero validated learning is genuinely dangerous. But clarify that the veto is not a delay mechanism. It's a circuit breaker. It doesn't prevent shipping; it prevents the specific failure mode where degradation accumulates past the point of recovery while three departments are still negotiating whether the threshold was actually breached. The question isn't 'ship or don't ship' — it's 'who has the authority to pull the emergency brake when the metrics themselves are unreliable?'"
